# Q7-Agent Report: MRT CLI Polish Audit
Date: 2026-04-05
Scope: src/bin/mirr-audit.rs, src/bin/mirr-brain.rs, src/bin/mirr-wave.rs, src/bin/mirr-general.rs, src/bin/mirr-lsp.rs

Primary question: Is MRT polished across the five MRT CLI binaries?

## 1) Explicit Verdict
NO.

MRT is not yet polished as a unified CLI suite. There is partial maturity in individual binaries (especially mirr-brain and mirr-general), but cross-binary polish is inconsistent for JSON format controls, error-code discipline, help/version parity, bounded output policy, and NASA P10 compliance.

## 2) Required Commands Executed (Sequentially)
1. `rg -n "format.*json|--format|error_code|MAX_|forbid.*unsafe|version" src/bin/`
- Confirmed key hits for all five target binaries, including JSON handling in `mirr-audit`, `mirr-brain`, `mirr-general`; `version` metadata in clap-based binaries; and `MAX_*` bounds in `mirr-brain` and `mirr-general`.
2. `cargo.exe run --bin mirr-brain -- --help 2>&1`
- Initial terminal capture returned exit code 1 with no visible text. Re-run with output capture showed complete help text including `-h/--help` and `-V/--version`, confirming the flags are exposed at runtime.

